    "updated_at": "2017-03-09T10:28:53Z",
    "body": "FWIW I believe Chrome does not implement the 'location' side of this, and enforces the same origin policy just with the cross-origin access checks (if I understand things correctly). See [bug](https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=664681). Anyway, if/when Chrome does implement the spec, this change to make a uniform way of having immutable prototypes should make things easier. cc @verwaest",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
