    "body": "If we don't make the linked change to ES, then we might as well not use SetImmutablePrototype at all, as it does't buy us anything. (\"Return false\" is shorter than \"Return SetImmutablePrototype(...)\".) If we want to maintain a world where all specs use the same consistent mechanism, then changing ES is the way to go.\r\n\r\nCurrently Chrome, Safari, and Firefox all implement \"allow null to be set cross-origin\" for WindowProxy.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
